      "metalness": 0.6,
      "note": "2.0.0 (12 Nov 2026, Kereem: \"Fix the LAKE\"): Boulevard's water look unchanged (the `water` preset, shared/materials/water-ssr.js) in a closed basin of our own built from the outline (builder/sculpt/lake-basin.js): the outline is the coping's outer edge; the coping (kerb-concrete or wet-paving) runs inward by copingWidth, mitred at every corner by an exact polygon inset (builder/sculpt/clip.js, polyclip inside Turf 7.4.0), with rounded arrises, a drip edge and a 5 cm overhang; a vertical wall or a sloped bank (bankSlope) down to the floor `depth` below the water; the water `freeboard` below the coping top, so below the promenade (y = 0). r187 webgpu_water for the surface and webgpu_generator_city (SidewalkGenerator curbGeometry: a profile carried round an outline) for the coping. Boulevard's water was a flat sheet 0.06 m above the ground (1.0.0, reference/lake-water.js): the no-loss pixel rule against it is expected to fail for the changed look. main.js waterSimple: MeshPhysicalNodeMaterial({ color: 0x0b2830, roughness: 0.04, metalness: 0, clearcoat: 1, clearcoatRoughness: 0.03 }), normals texture(waterNormals, xz / 9 + t x (0.012, 0.007)) and (xz / 23 - t x (0.006, -0.009)), normalMap(scale 0.35), colorNode vec3(0.016, 0.07, 0.085) (colour #224b52 is its nearest sRGB byte), metalnessNode 0.6; buildWater: water.position.y = 0.06. ?watermesh=1 (the r187 WaterMesh) is not Boulevard's default and is not used. The outline is a 30 x 20 m lake.",
      "copingWidth": 0.5,
      "copingHeight": 0.2,
      "freeboard": 0.6,
      "depth": 0.8,
      "wallStyle": "wall",
      "bankSlope": 30,
      "coping": "kerb-concrete"
    }
  },
